"""八本书的 Zenodo 长描述（HTML）。重新上传时从此处取用。"""

DESC = {
    'entropy-spiral': '<p><b>中文摘要。</b>本著作提出“时间错配”诊断框架，用以解释现代社会为什么反复出现“知道了也来不及”的结构性失败。它不预测崩溃，只回答一个更可操作的问题：一个系统是否还来得及自救？当金融按秒、政治按周、信任按年、生态按十年运行时，错位不是暂时失调，而是结构。</p>\n<p><b>核心主张。</b>时间不是背景，而是变量。以时间错配 τ = T_min / T_available、可控性 C = T_policy / T_threat = 1/τ 度量“还来不来得及”。τ 小于 1 表示尚有余量；接近 1 表示任何意外都可能翻盘；远大于 1 表示再正确的方案也追不上问题。现代社会不是一个钟，而是许多转速不同的钟；困难不在某一个钟走得快，而在它们无法被同一机制协调。</p>\n<p><b>理论与应用。</b>全书以三根不可逆轴——Θ（租佃/抽取份额）、I（组织复杂度）、κ（地缘耦合）——加一条独立的时间轴，构成脆弱性诊断 V；并把“来不及”从道德问题改写为算术问题。应用覆盖急诊决策、产品召回、气候治理、金融稳定、公共卫生与个人时间预算。三个应用情景给出 τ 约 0.5、3.5、30，恰好对应框架的精确、发散与失效三种状态。</p>\n<p><b>诚实的学术纪律。</b>全书按 A/B/C 与甲/乙/丙双重分级；τ 只作事后诊断与序数比较，不作事前预测；V 的权重与数据口径逐项标注，并附数据质量评估表，明确区分“可复算”与“跨年代可比”；可证伪登记簿与数据缺口清单随书公开，包括对 WDI、UN Comtrade 等来源的口径风险说明。</p>\n<p><b>预测与诊断的边界。</b>本书不给出崩溃时点。社会中两个关键层次——制度时间（I₂）与认知时间（I₄）——不可独立测量，这既是框架的硬边界，也是它拒绝给出“预言”的理由。它提供的是一张可控性边界图：在 C 小于 1 时，理性策略是减小暴露、预设降级，而不是追求精确控制。</p>\n<p><b>学术特点。</b>完全开源：正文源文件、插图源文件、数值模型与构建脚本均在 GitHub 仓库中可复现（内容 CC BY 4.0，代码 MIT）；方法论透明：分级、口径与失效条件写在正文而非脚注；跨域诊断工具：时间预算五步闭环、优雅降级顺序表、三层责任划分，均可直接使用。</p>\n<p><b>版本信息。</b>2026-10-18 版：321 页、25 章、42 幅插图、附录 A—J；GitHub：github.com/lyp0746/entropy-spiral。所有版本提交、数据文件与脚本均可追溯。</p>\n<p><b>Abstract (English).</b> This work presents a diagnostic framework of temporal mismatch, explaining why modern societies repeatedly fail not from ignorance but from being too late. It does not predict collapse; it answers a more actionable question: can a system still save itself in time?</p>\n<p><b>Core thesis.</b> Time is a variable, not a background. Temporal mismatch τ = T_min / T_available and controllability C = T_policy / T_threat = 1/τ measure whether there is still room to act. Modern society is not one clock but many clocks running at different speeds; the difficulty is not that one clock runs fast, but that they cannot be coordinated by a single mechanism.</p>\n<p><b>Theory and applications.</b> Three irreversible axes — Θ (extraction share), I (organisational complexity), κ (geopolitical coupling) — plus an independent temporal axis yield a vulnerability diagnostic V, and rewrite “too late” as arithmetic rather than moral failure. Applications cover emergency triage, product recalls, climate governance, financial stability, public health and personal time budgets. Three scenarios give τ ≈ 0.5, 3.5 and 30, corresponding to precision, divergence and failure.</p>\n<p><b>Scholarly discipline.</b> Every claim carries an evidence grade (A/B/C) and a conceptual grade (甲/乙/丙). τ is diagnostic and ordinal only, never a point forecast. Weights and data sources are graded, with a data-quality table that separates reproducibility from cross-era comparability. A falsifiability register and a data-gap list are included.</p>\n<p><b>Boundaries.</b> No point predictions of collapse. Two layers — institutional time (I₂) and cognitive time (I₄) — cannot be measured independently; this is the hard boundary of the framework. What it offers is a map of the boundary of controllability: when C &lt; 1, the rational strategy is to reduce exposure and pre-plan graceful degradation.</p>\n<p><b>Features.</b> Fully open source: manuscript, figures, numerical models and build scripts are reproducible on GitHub (content CC BY 4.0, code MIT). Methodological transparency: grades, definitions and failure conditions are in the main text. Cross-domain tools: the five-step time-budget loop, the graceful-degradation order, and the three-layer responsibility split.</p>\n<p><b>Edition.</b> 2026-10-18: 321 pages, 25 chapters, 42 figures, appendices A–J. GitHub: github.com/lyp0746/entropy-spiral. All commits, data files and scripts are traceable.</p>',
    'capacity-cascade': '<p><b>中文摘要。</b>本著作提出“容量级联”框架，用以解释有限容量如何同时塑造记忆、智能与自我。大语言模型的键值缓存、AI 智能体的上下文窗口与人的记忆—学习系统，是否由同一机制主导？本书给出的是一次有意的降级：三者不是同构，而是同约束。</p>\n<p><b>核心主张。</b>三个系统受同一组信息论约束——有限通道容量下的压缩、干扰与遗忘——却运行在相差约九个数量级的时间尺度上，形成从毫秒（工作记忆）到终身（系统巩固）的容量级联。遗忘因此不是记忆的失败，而是学习得以发生的前提：一个不肯丢信息的系统，也丢不掉噪声。</p>\n<p><b>理论与应用。</b>全书给出信息瓶颈、率失真、有效容量、表示坍塌与时间尺度分离的形式化，并把三种典型失败——位置偏差、上下文漂移、忒修斯现象——放在同一张表上比较。应用覆盖大模型上下文设计、智能体目标稳定性、睡眠与巩固、元认知与容量管理、教育与训练迁移、身份与伦理。</p>\n<p><b>实证与算例。</b>本版新增三组可复算实验：Hopfield 容量（负荷 α≈0.138 附近检索重叠由平台转入斜坡，而非断崖）、双时间尺度学习（仅当环境切换快于学习率时占优，约 3.8%，尺度变慢后无优势）、率失真曲线（精度提升的比特代价）。三组实验均给出参数、种子与失败记录。</p>\n<p><b>诚实的学术纪律。</b>同约束被写成三条可检验条件：C1 容量饱和、C2 双时间常数、C3 受限可塑性；任一条测不出，该载体即移出主张范围。“梦=正则化”等主张标为最低等级假说，并写明如何检验。双分级与可证伪登记簿随书公开，失败记录单独成节。</p>\n<p><b>预测与诊断的边界。</b>同约束不等于同构，跨载体的机制差异不可抹平；本书不主张“人脑与模型是同一个东西”，也不把容量曲线当作普适常数。它提供的是诊断坐标：在给定载体上，先测三条约束，再谈容量与遗忘。</p>\n<p><b>学术特点。</b>完全开源：实验脚本、数据、插图与构建流程可复现（CC BY 4.0 / MIT）。方法论透明：形式化定义、分级与数据缺口均在正文与附录中标明。设计工具：从“更大”到“更有效”的三个判据、容量仪表盘、记忆架构的取舍表。</p>\n<p><b>版本信息。</b>2026-10-18 版：203 页、25 章、31 幅插图、附录 A—K；GitHub：github.com/lyp0746/capacity-cascade。</p>\n<p><b>Abstract (English).</b> This work presents a “capacity cascade” framework explaining how finite capacity shapes memory, intelligence and the self at once. Are the KV cache of an LLM, the context window of an agent and human memory–learning governed by the same mechanism? The book argues for a deliberate demotion: not isomorphic, but iso-constrained.</p>\n<p><b>Core thesis.</b> The three systems are bound by one set of information-theoretic constraints — compression, interference and forgetting under finite capacity — while operating across roughly nine orders of magnitude, forming a capacity cascade from milliseconds (working memory) to a lifetime (systems consolidation). Forgetting is therefore the condition of learning, not its failure.</p>\n<p><b>Theory and applications.</b> The book formalises the information bottleneck, rate–distortion, effective capacity, representational collapse and timescale separation, and compares three characteristic failures — position bias, context drift, the Theseus phenomenon — in one table. Applications span context design, agent goal stability, sleep and consolidation, metacognition, education and identity.</p>\n<p><b>Empirical probes.</b> This edition adds three reproducible experiments: Hopfield capacity (retrieval overlap turns from a plateau into a slope near α≈0.138), two-timescale learning (advantage ≈3.8% only when the environment switches faster than the learning rate), and the rate–distortion curve. Parameters, seeds and failure records are included.</p>\n<p><b>Scholarly discipline.</b> Iso-constraint is operationalised as three testable conditions — capacity saturation, two time constants, constrained plasticity — and a carrier leaves the claim if any fails. The “dream as regularisation” claim is graded as a hypothesis with a stated test. Failures have their own section.</p>\n<p><b>Boundaries.</b> Iso-constraint is not isomorphism; the book does not claim that brains and models are the same thing, nor that the capacity curve is a universal constant. It offers diagnostic coordinates: measure the three constraints first, then talk about capacity and forgetting.</p>\n<p><b>Features.</b> Fully open source (CC BY 4.0 / MIT). Transparent methodology with explicit data gaps. Design tools: three criteria for “more effective rather than larger”, a capacity dashboard, and a trade-off table for memory architectures.</p>\n<p><b>Edition.</b> 2026-10-18: 203 pages, 25 chapters, 31 figures, appendices A–K. GitHub: github.com/lyp0746/capacity-cascade.</p>',
    'distinction-evolution': "<p><b>中文摘要。</b>本著作提出“区分的语法”这一语言规范，用以把“统一”从愿望翻译成可检验的操作。现代数学的统一冲动，可以被压缩成两个词：区分，与对称双线性形式。</p>\n<p><b>核心主张。</b>把“区分、曲率、演化”三个原语收敛为两个更基本的词——区分与对称双线性形式（二次型）；协方差、Hessian、图拉普拉斯、内积与黎曼度量是同一结构在五个领域的实例。曲率是形式谱的一个侧写，演化是形式谱上的线性方程。本书不宣布数学被统一，只交出一种可被使用、压缩与迁移的语言。</p>\n<p><b>理论与应用。</b>全书从“压缩：抽象如何统摄具体”讲到四场统一的交汇，再进入结构语言、二次型、形式决定群与图上相变。应用包括：微分形式对四个积分定理的统摄、从区分生成空间、非标准分析与超有限降级、类型与范畴中的相等层级，以及二十七个领域的区分结构编码。</p>\n<p><b>实证与算例。</b>唯一的完全兑现处是图上两阶段相变：局部（高频）模式先于全局（Fiedler）模式解锁，且对称边权下顺序不反转——有定理、有临界值、有可复算数值。本版新增局部先行窗口的尺度律 R = λmax/λ₂ ≈ 2N^{2/d}/π²，数值验证一维指数 2.00、二维 0.99。其余领域为结构相似而非同构，书中逐处标明。</p>\n<p><b>诚实的学术纪律。</b>明确区分“定理”“语言规范”与“提案”；19 个开放问题（O1—O19）；一次撤回（曲率与谱关系的过度归并）完整记录在正文与附录；并写明本书做的是“用已有工具描述已知结构”，不是“发明新工具发现新现象”。</p>\n<p><b>预测与诊断的边界。</b>五个领域中只有一个被严格兑现，其余为编码保持的结构相似；“语言规范”指可操作的记号系统，不是学科规范。把“同一结构”读成“已统一”，会高估它；读成“换了个说法”，会低估它。</p>\n<p><b>学术特点。</b>完全开源：证明、数据与可复算脚本公开（CC BY 4.0 / MIT）。方法论透明：分级、缺口与失败尝试均记录。工具：编码保结构的四级定义、两阶段相变的临界值表、局部窗口的尺度律。</p>\n<p><b>版本信息。</b>2026-10-18 版：223 页、25 章、33 幅插图、附录 A—P、O1—O19；GitHub：github.com/lyp0746/distinction-evolution。</p>\n<p><b>Abstract (English).</b> This work presents “the grammar of distinction,” a language norm that translates the wish for unity into testable operations. The unifying impulse of modern mathematics can be compressed into two words: distinction, and the symmetric bilinear form.</p>\n<p><b>Core thesis.</b> Three primitives — distinction, curvature, evolution — reduce to two: distinction and the symmetric bilinear form (quadratic form). Covariance, Hessian, graph Laplacian, inner product and Riemannian metric are five instances of one structure; curvature is a profile of the form's spectrum, evolution a linear equation on it. The book does not claim that mathematics has been unified; it delivers a language that can be used, compressed and transferred.</p>\n<p><b>Theory and applications.</b> From compression and four unification programmes to structural language, quadratic forms, forms determining groups, and phase transitions on graphs. Applications include differential forms subsuming four integral theorems, generating space from distinction, nonstandard analysis and hyperfinite descent, equality in type and category, and a coding of distinction structures across twenty-seven fields.</p>\n<p><b>Evidence.</b> The one fully cashed-out case is the two-stage transition on graphs: local (high-frequency) modes unlock before the global (Fiedler) mode, and the order cannot reverse under symmetric weights — theorem, thresholds, reproducible numbers. This edition adds the window law R = λmax/λ₂ ≈ 2N^{2/d}/π², verified with exponents 2.00 (1D) and 0.99 (2D). Elsewhere the relation is structural resemblance, marked as such.</p>\n<p><b>Discipline.</b> Theorems, language norms and proposals are kept apart; 19 open questions; one retraction is documented in full; the book states that it describes known structures with existing tools rather than discovering new phenomena with new ones.</p>\n<p><b>Boundaries.</b> Only one of five domains is fully cashed out; “norm” means notation, not disciplinary rule. Reading the claim as “mathematics unified” overestimates it; reading it as “a restatement” underestimates it.</p>\n<p><b>Features.</b> Fully open source (CC BY 4.0 / MIT), with proofs, data and scripts. Transparent methodology with gaps and failed attempts recorded. Tools: four-level coding definitions, threshold tables, and the window scaling law.</p>\n<p><b>Edition.</b> 2026-10-18: 223 pages, 25 chapters, 33 figures, appendices A–P, O1–O19. GitHub: github.com/lyp0746/distinction-evolution.</p>",
    'impossibility-triangle': "<p><b>中文摘要。</b>本著作提出“选择的代价”诊断框架，用以阐释任何有限复杂度知识系统的形成、演化与更新所面临的结构性困境。它不提出新的统一机制，而是给出一条约束：完备、可组合、跨尺度传递，三者不能同时充分具备。</p>\n<p><b>核心主张。</b>任何试图描述多尺度复杂系统的知识框架，都面临一个不可突破的三角约束：<b>完备性（C）</b>——各部分具有自洽、精确的描述与预测；<b>可组合性（A）</b>——子系统的组合不产生新的非线性项，能力可叠加；<b>跨尺度传递性（T）</b>——不同尺度的结论可无损互推，因果链可穿透尺度边界。系统至多能充分保有其中两项；选择任意两项，第三项必然留下可定位的缺口。三角不是宿命，而是一张价目表：它不告诉你“不行”，它告诉你“这样东西要花多少”。</p>\n<p><b>理论与应用。</b>本书是系列六本专著中的第四部，统一整合前三部：《遗忘的边界》（C+T 困境）、《区分的语法》（C+A 困境）、《错位的时间》（A+T 困境）。全书以信息子模性、离散—连续断层（1/3 缺口）与时间错配 τ 作为三角约束的三条理论见证。框架被系统应用于六个领域：医疗（个体化诊断与群体指南的协调）、教育（学生自主性与国家标准的政策摇摆）、组织（CEO／员工／股东／监管的代理冲突）、金融（流动性、风险、效率的三角，LTCM 1998 案例）、软件工程（涌现缺陷与模块化发展的尺度传递）、人工智能（泛化能力与样本复杂度的预测边界）。</p>\n<p><b>实证基础。</b>本版包含三项可复现的实证探针，用真实数据与开源脚本检验框架自身的预测能力。<b>软件仓库双对照：</b>同一假设“跨子系统改动审批更慢”，在 Linux 内核 commit 量度上不被支持（Spearman r = −0.098，p = 0.168，95% CI 跨 0），在 Node.js 的 PR merge 量度上被强支持（r = +0.251，p = 0.0003，CI 不含 0）——结论高度依赖量度选择。<b>文献网络探针：</b>用 arXiv 1995—2023 数据检验“学科分裂导致跨领域耦合下降”，结果方向相反：跨分类论文占比由 0.17 升至 0.54，朴素预测被反驳。<b>引用层面复核：</b>改用 OpenAlex 的跨领域引用占比后，只有计算机科学下降（0.42→0.16），物理呈 U 形、神经科学 2020 反弹——分裂主张只在一个领域被支持。三个探针合起来，构成“一个被支持、一个不可判、一个方向相反”的完整记录。</p>\n<p><b>诚实的学术纪律。</b>全书 37 个可证伪的开放问题（O1—O37），明确标注哪些已证、哪些是框架假设、哪些待验证；所有主张按 A/B/C 与甲/乙/丙双重分级；预测失效与量度污染写在正文（如 Linux 时延代理的教训）；曾被推翻的强主张保留在附录，展示框架演化而非最终真理；并有一次完整的独立性协议与失败案例集。</p>\n<p><b>预测与诊断的边界。</b>框架达到 L2—L3 预测水平：能说“失效的形态与方向”，不能说“新配置、触发点与时点”。这不是缺陷，而是“有限复杂度约束”在预测层面的表现。框架的价值在于让设计者与决策者看清“选择两项时第三项会如何失效”，从而做更诚实的权衡，而不是提供一键诊断或因果确定性。</p>\n<p><b>学术特点。</b>完全开源：计算脚本、数据处理、绘图代码与正文源文件均在 GitHub 可复现（内容 CC BY 4.0，代码 MIT）；方法论透明：数据质量自评、因果推论局限、量度有效性检验；跨域诊断工具：“边界敏感性检查”“代理权力矩阵”“失效分类与容限”等可直接使用；研究纲领：明确定位为诊断框架，不替代领域专业判断。</p>\n<p><b>版本信息。</b>2026-10-18 版：272 页、25 章、38 幅插图、附录 A—Y、O1—O37；GitHub：github.com/lyp0746/impossibility-triangle。所有版本提交、数据文件与脚本均可追溯。</p>\n<p><b>Abstract (English).</b> This work presents “The Price of Choice,” a diagnostic framework explaining the structural dilemma inherent in the formation, evolution and updating of any finite-complexity knowledge system. It offers not a new unifying mechanism but a constraint.</p>\n<p><b>Core thesis.</b> Any framework describing multiscale complex systems faces an unbreakable triadic constraint: it cannot simultaneously and fully possess <b>completeness (C)</b> — each component has a self-consistent, precise description and predictive capacity; <b>composability (A)</b> — combining subsystems generates no new nonlinear terms, so capabilities stack; and <b>transitive cross-scale coherence (T)</b> — conclusions across scales can be interpenetrated losslessly, causal chains are scale-transparent. A system can adequately maintain at most two; choosing any two leaves a locatable gap at the third vertex. The triangle is not fate but a price list: it does not say “you cannot”, it says “this is what it costs”.</p>\n<p><b>Theory and applications.</b> The fourth of six monographs in the series, it unifies the previous three: The Boundary of Forgetting (the C+T dilemma), The Grammar of Distinction (the C+A gap), and Desynchronized Time (the A+T trade-off). Information submodularity, the discrete–continuous gap (1/3), and temporal mismatch τ serve as theoretical witnesses. Applications span medicine, education, organisations, finance (LTCM 1998), software engineering, and AI.</p>\n<p><b>Empirical foundation.</b> Three reproducible probes test the framework's own predictions. A dual-repository software analysis tests “cross-module changes face longer approval delays”: unsupported on Linux commits (Spearman r = −0.098, p = 0.168, CI spanning zero) but strongly supported on Node.js pull requests (r = +0.251, p = 0.0003). A literature-network probe on arXiv (1995–2023) contradicts the naive fragmentation prediction: cross-category papers rise from 0.17 to 0.54. A citation-level check with OpenAlex shows fragmentation only in computer science (0.42→0.16), a U-shape in physics and a 2020 rebound in neuroscience. Together: one supported, one inconclusive, one contrary.</p>\n<p><b>Scholarly discipline.</b> 37 falsifiable open questions (O1–O37) grade what is proved, assumed or untested; every claim carries an evidence grade (A/B/C) and a conceptual grade; failed predictions and measurement contamination are reported in the main text; retracted strong claims are kept, showing the framework's evolution rather than final truth.</p>\n<p><b>Boundaries.</b> The framework reaches L2–L3 predictive power — failure modalities and directions, not novel configurations, triggers or timing. This is the expression of the finite-complexity constraint at the level of prediction, not a deficiency. Its value is to let designers see how the third property breaks when two are chosen.</p>\n<p><b>Features.</b> Fully open source (CC BY 4.0 / MIT); transparent methodology (data grading, causal limits, measurement validity checks); operational tools (boundary-sensitivity audit, agent power matrix, failure classification); explicitly a diagnostic framework, not a substitute for domain expertise.</p>\n<p><b>Edition.</b> 2026-10-18: 272 pages, 25 chapters, 38 figures, appendices A–Y, O1–O37. GitHub: github.com/lyp0746/impossibility-triangle.</p>",
    'interpretation-tradeoff': '<p><b>中文摘要。</b>本著作提出“诠释即置信度分配”的诊断框架，用以解释历史学为什么在材料不断增加时仍然争吵不休。它不谈“历史是什么”，而是诊断“诠释在做什么”。</p>\n<p><b>核心主张。</b>诠释就是给一组互相竞争的命题分配置信度：“他确实说过这句话”置信度高，“他因此被排挤”置信度中，“这标志一个时代的转向”置信度低。一个诠释的形状，由这组置信度的分布决定。由此，客观性被拆成四个可检验的层次——观察、推理、诠释、因果——每层各有自己的证据标准与可接受的反驳。</p>\n<p><b>理论与应用。</b>全书给出最小内核（置信度分配）、四层结构、C-A-T 在史学中的具体让出，并以五个应用展开：人物还原与贝叶斯更新、跨文明制度比较、帝国衰落与“大分流”、科学诞生与法国大革命、唐宋变革与分期之争；再以“框架在放大时如何退化”收束，指出在历史这类对象上诊断只能到隐喻一级。</p>\n<p><b>实证与算例。</b>本版包含两组可复算示范。其一是先验敏感性：同一组似然、不同先验，可以得出相反结论（0.488 / 0.366 / 0.146 对 0.340 / 0.412 / 0.248）；其二是编码敏感性：弱效应叠加边界案例时，约 8.9% 的数据集会被“合理但不同”的编码翻转结论，而强效应下低于 1%。两者都说明：结论的稳定度取决于先验与量度，而不只取决于材料。</p>\n<p><b>诚实的学术纪律。</b>每条判断标注层级与强度；把一次失败——把 C-A-T 位置形式化为可计算不等式的尝试被撤回——写进正文第 5.6 节而非只放附录；开放问题、可证伪登记簿与自诊工作表随书公开；每章附“可反驳条件”与“谁在付代价”。</p>\n<p><b>预测与诊断的边界。</b>置信度分配可以被操作化，但“三角位置”在史学中尚不能独立测量；在历史对象上，诊断只能到隐喻级。本书不提供“历史规律”，也不把位置冲突读成“没有真相”——它说的是：真相有，但带着置信度、尺度与位置。</p>\n<p><b>学术特点。</b>完全开源：源文件、数据与脚本可复现（CC BY 4.0 / MIT）；方法论透明：四层分级、先验标注、失败记录；工具：置信度分配工作表、编码敏感性自查、五问清单，可直接用于研究与教学。</p>\n<p><b>版本信息。</b>2026-10-18 版：204 页、25 章、21 幅插图、附录 A—AC；GitHub：github.com/lyp0746/interpretation-tradeoff。</p>\n<p><b>Abstract (English).</b> This work presents a diagnostic framework: interpretation is the allocation of confidence to competing propositions. Rather than asking what history is, it diagnoses what interpretation does.</p>\n<p><b>Core thesis.</b> “He did say it” carries high confidence, “he was therefore marginalised” medium, “this marks a turning point of an age” low; the shape of an interpretation is the distribution of those confidences. Objectivity is broken into four testable layers — observation, inference, interpretation, causation — each with its own evidential standard and admissible rebuttal.</p>\n<p><b>Theory and applications.</b> The book develops the minimal core, the four layers, and the specific give-ups of C-A-T in historiography, then applies them to person restoration and Bayesian updating, cross-civilisational comparison, imperial decline and the Great Divergence, the birth of science and the French Revolution, and the Tang–Song periodisation debate; it closes with how the framework degrades when scaled up, conceding that for objects like history diagnosis reaches only metaphor.</p>\n<p><b>Demonstrations.</b> Two reproducible demonstrations. Prior sensitivity: the same likelihoods with different priors yield opposite conclusions (0.488/0.366/0.146 versus 0.340/0.412/0.248). Coding sensitivity: with weak effects and borderline cases, about 8.9% of datasets flip under reasonable coding, versus under 1% for strong effects. Stability depends on priors and measures, not only on materials.</p>\n<p><b>Discipline.</b> Every judgement carries its layer and strength; one failure — the attempt to formalise C-A-T positions — is reported in the main text (5.6), not buried in an appendix; worksheets and a falsifiability register are included; each chapter names a refutation condition and who pays the cost.</p>\n<p><b>Boundaries.</b> Confidence allocation is operational; triangle positions are not yet independently measurable. For history, diagnosis reaches only metaphor. The book offers no “laws of history”, and does not read positional conflict as “no truth” — truth exists, with confidence, scale and position attached.</p>\n<p><b>Features.</b> Fully open source (CC BY 4.0 / MIT); transparent method (four layers, prior labelling, failure records); tools: a confidence-allocation worksheet, a coding-sensitivity self-check, and a five-question checklist for research and teaching.</p>\n<p><b>Edition.</b> 2026-10-18: 204 pages, 25 chapters, 21 figures, appendices A–AC. GitHub: github.com/lyp0746/interpretation-tradeoff.</p>',
    'emergence-critical': '<p><b>中文摘要。</b>本著作提出“临界”的可操作定义与检验程序，用以回答一个古老但含混的问题：变化究竟在哪一刻，从“还是原来的东西”变成“另一个东西”？</p>\n<p><b>核心主张。</b>一次质变＝系统在某个尺度上获得不可由微观无损推出的宏观序。它有三个可观测标记：序参量跃变、临界慢化、宏观描述比细节更好用；三个中两个成立，才叫质变。临界不是第六个并列概念，而是前五个核心共同作用时出现的那道门槛。</p>\n<p><b>理论与应用。</b>全书从“量变到质变为什么需要一门科学”开始，给出六件工具（序参量、对称破缺、临界慢化、标度与普适类、因果涌现、下向因果），再以五步流程与反例检验前五本书：区分、遗忘、时间、取舍、诠释。最后把视角推向形式化的地平线、不可通约、以及“不要把地平线当台阶”的警告。</p>\n<p><b>实证与算例。</b>本版包含四组可复算实验。二维 Ising 蒙特卡洛校准：T_c = 2.2645（精确 2.26919）、γ/ν = 1.752（精确 1.75）；β/ν = 0.156 偏大 25%、ν 未测出，均如实报告。临界雪崩：m=1.0 时幂律指数 1.495（理论 3/2）。临界慢化：AR(1) 的恢复时间与方差在 5% 内吻合。有限尺度坍缩：同一批数据，少一个尺寸就可能翻转判定——这成为“诊断效力随尺度增长”的核心证据。</p>\n<p><b>诚实的学术纪律。</b>六个最小验证单元按“能不能真做”排序，并标明哪些已做、哪些只到部分通过；失败记录单独成节（附录 R）；每张图都配脚本与随机种子；被合并章节中遗漏的推导（朗道、标度、KKT）恢复为附录 X，并注明是“补编”而非新内容。</p>\n<p><b>预测与诊断的边界。</b>多数社会案例只能到隐喻级；单一指标不能定向；慢化报“近”，不报“何时”。框架的核心发现不是一条新常数，而是一条边界：诊断的效力与可观测尺度成正比——尺度不够时，两个竞争假设会一样好看。</p>\n<p><b>学术特点。</b>完全开源：实验脚本、数据、插图与构建流程可复现（CC BY 4.0 / MIT）；方法论透明：分级、失败与“事后补算”均标注；工具：一页纸诊断表、六件工具速查、十个案例的对照打分。</p>\n<p><b>版本信息。</b>2026-10-18 版：213 页、25 章、15 幅插图、附录 A—X；GitHub：github.com/lyp0746/emergence-critical。</p>\n<p><b>Abstract (English).</b> This work offers an operational definition and test procedure for criticality, answering an old but vague question: at which moment does a change turn from “the same thing” into “another thing”?</p>\n<p><b>Core thesis.</b> A qualitative transition is the emergence, at some scale, of macro-order that cannot be derived losslessly from the micro-level. It has three observable markers — order-parameter jump, critical slowing down, and macro-description being more useful than detail; two out of three are required. Criticality is not a sixth parallel concept but the threshold that appears when the first five cores act together.</p>\n<p><b>Theory and applications.</b> Six tools (order parameter, symmetry breaking, critical slowing down, scaling and universality, causal emergence, downward causation), a five-step procedure, and a test of the previous five books: distinction, forgetting, time, choice and interpretation. The book then moves to the horizon of formalisation, incommensurability, and the warning against mistaking a horizon for a step.</p>\n<p><b>Experiments.</b> Four reproducible experiments. 2D Ising Monte Carlo: T_c = 2.2645 (exact 2.26919), γ/ν = 1.752 (exact 1.75); β/ν = 0.156 (25% high) and ν unresolved, both reported. Critical avalanches: exponent 1.495 at m=1.0 (theory 3/2). Slowing down: AR(1) relaxation time and variance within 5%. Finite-size collapse: with one size fewer, the verdict can flip — the central evidence that diagnostic power scales with the observable scale.</p>\n<p><b>Discipline.</b> Six minimal verification units are ordered by feasibility and marked done, partial or open; failures have their own appendix; every figure ships with a script and a seed; derivations lost in an earlier merge (Landau, scaling, KKT) are restored as Appendix X and labelled as supplements.</p>\n<p><b>Boundaries.</b> Most social cases reach only metaphor; a single indicator cannot orient; slowing down reports “near”, not “when”. The central finding is a boundary, not a constant: diagnostic power scales with the observable scale.</p>\n<p><b>Features.</b> Fully open source (CC BY 4.0 / MIT); transparent method with grades, failures and post-hoc computations marked; tools: a one-page diagnostic sheet, a six-tool quick reference, and a ten-case scoring table.</p>\n<p><b>Edition.</b> 2026-10-18: 213 pages, 25 chapters, 15 figures, appendices A–X. GitHub: github.com/lyp0746/emergence-critical.</p>',
    'knowledge-tradeoffs': "<p><b>中文摘要。</b>本著作是“有限系统的取舍”系列的入口读本：用六个核心，把六本学术专著写成一本从十岁到专家都能读完的书。它同时承担系列的外部登记库功能——最小可验证单元、跨域盲测登记、合并术语表都收在这里。</p>\n<p><b>核心主张。</b>看得见的世界背后，都有一张看不见的账单；账单上只有三个价格——看得准、拼得上、传得下去，最多付得起两个。让出的那一个，就是每一章要指认的东西。六个核心——<b>看见</b>（区分）、<b>记住</b>（容量）、<b>跟上</b>（时间）、<b>选择</b>（C-A-T）、<b>讲述</b>（置信度）、<b>临界</b>（门槛）——不是六门学问，而是同一笔账的六个项目。</p>\n<p><b>结构与方法。</b>全书 19 部、121 页。每一部都配“三个小故事”与“动手试试”；同一段内容同时提供四种高度：故事给所有人，“多想一层”给学生（一个公式加一句直觉），“再想一层”给从业者（这条结论有多硬、能做什么、不能做什么），“给专家的注”给研究者（精确陈述、原始章节、证据等级、如何反驳）。另设练习册、常见误解、给老师／家长／孩子的一页、二十五个真实的人、三十个用法、一场三个人的谈话、一年之后的复盘。</p>\n<p><b>与专著的关系。</b>六个核心分别对应六本专著：《区分的语法》《遗忘的边界》《错位的时间》《选择的代价》《诠释的权衡》《涌现的临界》。本书不新增实证结论；凡通俗化损伤原意之处，以专著为准；每一处可复算的数字都注明来源与等级。</p>\n<p><b>诚实的学术纪律。</b>六个核心各自标明对应专著的证据等级；分级装置（A/B/C 与甲/乙/丙）在正文以“括号 + 一句话”的方式出现，不堆叠免责；每部结尾的“边界”写清这一部不能回答什么；书中保留失败与反例（例如“六个核心也会漏东西”）。</p>\n<p><b>预测与诊断的边界。</b>它是入口，不是替代；它给坐标与工具，不给判决。读者若只带走一句话，应是：“没有东西能装下所有东西，所以要学会选择——而且可以选得明白。”</p>\n<p><b>学术特点。</b>完全开源：正文源文件、插图与构建流程可复现（CC BY 4.0 / MIT）；四种读者的分层经过实际试读与改写；工具：六核速查表、练习册、读书会指南（六次，每次一小时）、给老师的一节课方案。</p>\n<p><b>版本信息。</b>2026-10-18 版：121 页、19 部、29 幅插图；GitHub：github.com/lyp0746/knowledge-tradeoffs。系列入口与外部登记库同址。</p>\n<p><b>Abstract (English).</b> This is the entry volume of the “Tradeoffs of Finite Systems” series: six core ideas turn six monographs into a book readable from age ten to specialist. It also serves as the series' external registry — minimal verification units, cross-domain blind-test registration, and a merged glossary.</p>\n<p><b>Core thesis.</b> Behind the visible world lies an invisible bill with three prices — being precise, fitting together, and carrying over — and at most two can be paid. The six cores — <b>seeing</b> (distinction), <b>remembering</b> (capacity), <b>keeping up</b> (time), <b>choosing</b> (C-A-T), <b>telling</b> (confidence), <b>criticality</b> (threshold) — are six items on one bill, not six disciplines.</p>\n<p><b>Structure.</b> 19 parts, 121 pages. Each part carries three short stories and a hands-on exercise, and offers four depths at once: story for everyone, “one layer deeper” for students (a formula plus intuition), “one more layer” for practitioners (how hard the claim is, what it can and cannot do), and “note for experts” (precise statement, source chapter, evidence grade, how to refute). A workbook, common misconceptions, a page for teachers, parents and children, twenty-five real people, thirty usages, a three-person conversation and a one-year retrospective complete the volume.</p>\n<p><b>Relation to the monographs.</b> The six cores map one-to-one onto six monographs. The book adds no new empirical claims; where popularisation distorts the original, the monograph prevails; every computable number carries its source and grade.</p>\n<p><b>Discipline.</b> Each core names the evidence grade of its source monograph; grades appear as a bracketed phrase, not as stacked disclaimers; each part ends with what it cannot answer; failures and counterexamples are kept (including “the six cores also miss things”).</p>\n<p><b>Boundaries.</b> It is an entry point, not a substitute: coordinates and tools, not verdicts. If a reader takes one sentence away, it should be: “nothing can hold everything, so learn to choose — and choose with your eyes open.”</p>\n<p><b>Features.</b> Fully open source (CC BY 4.0 / MIT); the four reader levels were tested in reading; tools include a six-core quick reference, the workbook, a six-session reading-group guide, and a one-lesson plan for teachers.</p>\n<p><b>Edition.</b> 2026-10-18: 121 pages, 19 parts, 29 figures. GitHub: github.com/lyp0746/knowledge-tradeoffs.</p>",
    'hotspot-bills': "<p><b>中文摘要。</b>本著作是系列的方法演示：用六个核心，把过去一年被反复讨论的公共事件做成一张张“诊断卡”。它不判对错，只诊断这场争论卡在哪一层、让出了什么、谁在付账。</p>\n<p><b>核心主张。</b>热搜为什么总让人越看越看不懂？因为讨论被压缩、被分层、被时间错配，而读者往往在错误的楼层里找答案。六把尺子——<b>看见</b>（在划什么线、谁被排除）、<b>记住</b>（被压成什么标签、丢了什么）、<b>跟上</b>（快钟与慢钟差多少）、<b>选择</b>（各方要哪两样、让出哪一样）、<b>讲述</b>（争事实还是抢位置）、<b>临界</b>（还是原来那个东西吗）——不问“谁对”，只问“卡在哪”。</p>\n<p><b>数据与方法。</b>案例全部来自真实公开存档：知乎热榜每日存档，2025-10-16 至 2026-10-16，338 天、2875 个不同话题；X 趋势按国家按日期的历史存档，美／英／日，81 个“国家—日”采样。全书 18 章、100 页，含 71 张诊断卡（65 张标准卡、5 张长卡、30 条一句话诊断），另有季度复盘、方法自检、十个反例、一个 90 分钟工作坊与数据附录。</p>\n<p><b>实证与算例。</b>季度复盘用脚本统计四季度天数、话题日总数、前五占比，并如实标注 Q4 缺日、不可比总量；数据附录列出各季前 30 名；每张卡都带证据等级与可反驳条件；十个反例逐条说明“什么情况下这张卡是错的”。</p>\n<p><b>诚实的学术纪律。</b>诊断的是讨论的结构，不是事件的对错；数据缺口与口径问题逐条写明；平台数据的局限（平台≠公众、热度≠重要性、天数≠因果）写在正文；“上榜天数”只作代理变量，并给出其失效条件。</p>\n<p><b>预测与诊断的边界。</b>案例会过期，方法不会；它不预测、不判决，也不替代一手来源。它提供的是一个可以重算的诊断流程：选事件、填六格、写可反驳条件、三个月后对账。</p>\n<p><b>学术特点。</b>完全开源：采集与统计脚本、原始数据、插图与构建流程可复现（CC BY 4.0 / MIT）；方法论透明：每个数字都能由脚本重新得到；工具：诊断卡模板、六核速查、一页纸诊断表、90 分钟工作坊流程。</p>\n<p><b>版本信息。</b>2026-10-18 版：100 页、18 章、8 幅插图、71 张诊断卡；GitHub：github.com/lyp0746/hotspot-bills。</p>\n<p><b>Abstract (English).</b> This is the series' methodological demonstration: six cores turn a year of contested public events into diagnostic cards. It does not judge right or wrong; it diagnoses on which layer the argument is stuck, what it gives up, and who pays.</p>\n<p><b>Core thesis.</b> Why does the hot list leave us more confused the longer we look? Because discussion is compressed, layered and temporally misaligned, while readers look for answers on the wrong floor. Six lenses — <b>seeing</b> (what line is drawn, who is excluded), <b>remembering</b> (what label survives, what is lost), <b>keeping up</b> (how far apart the fast and slow clocks are), <b>choosing</b> (which two each side wants, which one it gives up), <b>telling</b> (facts or positions), <b>criticality</b> (is it still the same thing) — ask not “who is right” but “where is it stuck”.</p>\n<p><b>Data and method.</b> All cases come from real public archives: daily Zhihu hot-list archives, 2025-10-16 to 2026-10-16, 338 days and 2,875 distinct topics; X trend archives by country and date for the US, UK and Japan, 81 country–day samples. 18 chapters, 100 pages, 71 diagnostic cards (65 standard, 5 long-form, 30 one-line), plus a quarterly review, a method self-audit, ten counterexamples, a 90-minute workshop and data appendices.</p>\n<p><b>Evidence.</b> The quarterly review computes days, topic-days and top-five shares by script, and states plainly that Q4 has missing days and cannot be compared on totals; appendices list the top 30 per quarter; every card carries an evidence grade and a refutation condition; ten counterexamples state when each card is wrong.</p>\n<p><b>Discipline.</b> The object of diagnosis is the structure of the argument, not the facts of the case; data gaps and measurement caveats are stated; platform limitations (platform ≠ public, heat ≠ importance, days ≠ causation) are in the main text; “days on the list” is only a proxy, with its failure conditions given.</p>\n<p><b>Boundaries.</b> Cases expire, the method does not; it neither predicts nor judges, and never replaces primary sources. It offers a recomputable procedure: pick an event, fill six cells, write a refutation condition, check back in three months.</p>\n<p><b>Features.</b> Fully open source (CC BY 4.0 / MIT): collection and statistics scripts, raw data, figures and build pipeline; transparent methodology: every number can be recomputed; tools: a card template, a six-lens quick reference, a one-page diagnostic sheet, and a 90-minute workshop.</p>\n<p><b>Edition.</b> 2026-10-18: 100 pages, 18 chapters, 8 figures, 71 diagnostic cards. GitHub: github.com/lyp0746/hotspot-bills.</p>",
}
